<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena and other unilocular tests vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 2) — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring maps E3-E8 and the comparators to pages 216-263; every model function names its equation; the decision rule is spelled out with its three constants; the math KG YAML and Lean module cite v2 line ranges. The constants 0.06 / 1.5 / 0.10 / 0.12 remain judgement calls, now documented as such." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py L112–L115: gate constants are stated, not derived from a noise model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a1dca587c/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L112-L115>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena and other unilocular tests vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 2) — Model fidelity to source: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Catalogue implemented from the Kenmotsu first-integral form with all five members and the correct limits, self-tested against the root identities, the elliptic period and the closed-form flask join radius; 18 Lean theorems (0 sorry) check the integer algebra including the bead aspect bound and join feasibility. The sphere+cylinder ablation shows the unduloid shoulder is load-bearing (17/18 tests fit worse without it). Deductions: join is C1 not C2, neck has no apertural lip, the nodoid branch is characterised in the sweep but not offered as a fit model." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py L503–L526: parameter_sweep characterises the nodoid (B > 1) but MODELS has no nodoid fit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a1dca587c/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L503-L526>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena and other unilocular tests vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 2) — Morphometric validation: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every silhouette gets nRMSE, Pearson r, KS statistic and 2-fold CV for five models; the Delaunay residual is judged against the per-specimen free-form floor (capped at 0.10) rather than a fixed number; the ellipsoid null (median 0.116) and the sphere+cylinder ablation (0.148) are both clearly worse than Delaunay (0.057); photograph sizes are calibrated from the scale bars (Lagena 186-276 um, Oolina 224 um, Fissurina 204-227 um) and cross-checked against the typical unilocular size range. Deductions: n = 2 negative controls, one of which passes; KS p-values are dominated by the row count and only the statistic is informative; no published Lagena outline morphometrics exist to compare the fitted B distribution against." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py L99–L107: only two polythalamous control panels <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a1dca587c/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L99-L107>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-delaunay-compatible-unilocular-tests>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-fitted-kenmotsu-b-range>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-flask-like-tests-l-w-pi-delaunay-compatible>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-lagena-sp-test-length-from-100-um-scale-bar>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-2-fold-cv-rmse-r-max-best-delaunay>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-best-delaunay-rmse-r-max-tests>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-bilateral-asymmetry-index-mean-r-l-r-r-r-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-ellipsoid-null-rmse-r-max-tests>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-ks-statistic-observed-vs-fitted-radii-best-delaunay>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-pearson-r-observed-vs-fitted-radius>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-sphere-cylinder-ablation-rmse-r-max-tests>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-polythalamous-negative-controls-delaunay-compatible>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-spindle-tests-l-w-pi-delaunay-compatible>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-tests-where-delaunay-beats-the-ellipsoid-null>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-unilocular-test-silhouettes-analysed-13-drawings-5-photographs>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena and other unilocular tests vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 73.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "v2 keeps the exact Delaunay catalogue of v1 and adds everything Pass 1 lacked: the Kireenko (2022) CC-BY photographs are segmented (Otsu, largest component, plate-wide 100 um scale-bar calibration), each silhouette is fitted by E7 flask, E8 bead, an ellipsoid null, a sphere+cylinder ablation and a free-form degree-6 reference, with nRMSE, Pearson r, KS statistic and 2-fold CV; a B/t regime sweep tabulates the catalogue; polythalamous controls are run through the same pipeline; result.json records the verdict. Result: MIXED — 11/18 unilocular tests compatible (flask-like 11/13 at median nRMSE 0.050 vs free-form 0.049, null 0.116, ablation 0.148; spindles 0/5 at 0.209), Delaunay beats the ablation on 17/18 and the null on 13/18, 1/2 controls pass (specificity caveat). Overall 73.8/100. Overall 73.8/100 (faithfulness 70.3, reproducibility 81.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a1dca587c; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 62, Parameter expressivity 72, Morphometric validation 70, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 78. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_014_the_forms_of_cells_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py at a1dca587c, image/png, 1300317 B, 2200×2000 px, artifact_sha256 c1a3b83ef9c297102c4678e792cd32ff1bae61b390cdd49ee79afce34a46683e (sha256 c1a3b83ef9c297102c4678e792cd32ff1bae61b390cdd49ee79afce34a46683e), spec_fingerprint 96b8d320bb6057308c24557dd6f3e3dce73bc0bc00dfdf30f45d3f4ca513f1dc. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 96b8d320bb6057308c24557dd6f3e3dce73bc0bc00dfdf30f45d3f4ca513f1dc; artifact_sha256: c1a3b83ef9c297102c4678e792cd32ff1bae61b390cdd49ee79afce34a46683e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/kireenko_2022_bdj_e87457_fig8_station5656mc.jpg=3b57acc0dfc98374..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/paper_citations.bib=a21c514d2fded5d2..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/scout_manifest.json=53e6b01a4f0e6102..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/t1917_014_the_forms_of_cells_reference.json=0a5ac92486643991..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/thompson_1917_fig84_lagena_after_brady.png=c02d29af384791df..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/thompson_1917_leaf0276_p256_fig84.jp2=ed440583a8b144d5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) p. 256: Lagena shells are 'flask-shaped ... whose surface is simply that of an unduloid, or more frequently ... an unduloid combined with a portion of a sphere'; p. 218: the CMC surfaces of revolution are the plane, sphere, cylinder, catenoid, unduloid and nodoid; reconstructed_in_script: Kenmotsu (1980) parametrisation of the Delaunay family; C1 sphere-unduloid-cylinder flask and unduloid bead composites fitted by bounded least squares to the meridional radius profile of 13 Fig. 84 silhouettes and 7 photographed tests, compared against an ellipsoid null, a sphere+cylinder ablation and a free-form polynomial with nRMSE, Pearson r, KS statistic and 2-fold CV; transfer_boundary: The drawings are Brady's as redrawn in 1917; the photographs are 2-D side views of 3-D tests, so axisymmetry is tested only by bilateral symmetry of the outline; the outline test has limited specificity for egg-shaped shells (1/2 polythalamous controls pass); does_not_claim: No claim about the surface-tension mechanism (hanging drop); no claim about Nodosaria chains, Orbulina or non-foram protists; no claim that passing tests are uniquely Delaunay rather than merely consistent; n = 2 controls and n = 5 photographed unilocular tests are small samples." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — both passes are builder-scored'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R10', 'item': 'Derive the nRMSE gate from a segmentation-noise model (e.g. bootstrap over threshold 0.035-0.055) instead of fixed constants'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R11', 'item': 'Test the surface-of-revolution premise in 3-D (apertural views 61b/62b are nearly circular; quantify their circularity)'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8', 'item': 'More photographed unilocular tests (Kireenko 2022 Fig. 19: Lagena 112/113, Procerolagena 114, Oolina 115/116) and more polythalamous controls so the specificity caveat rests on n > 2'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R9', 'item': 'Offer the nodoid (B > 1) and the catenoid as fit models so every catalogue member is tested, not only characterised'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.38e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

