<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena and other unilocular tests vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 2) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Real specimens are now compared side by side (panels E-F): 4/5 photographed unilocular tests (Fissurina 57a/58a, Lagena 62a, Oolina 63) are traced by the Delaunay composite to within 0.018-0.051 nRMSE, Lagena 61a fails (0.083 vs free-form 0.018: its neck tapers like a cone rather than an unduloid), and the 13 drawings split flask/spindle as in Pass 1. Deductions: only one plate and five unilocular photographs; the egg-shaped Quinqueloculina control also matches, so the visual match is not specific to single-chambered tests; the drawn spindles are visibly not reproduced (the honest negative)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
